<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:43:43 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Houthi attacks and no Western support: What are Saudi Arabia's options ?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options</link><description>
The US has warned that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthis could rapidly escalate. It comes after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The Houthis' lightning offensive seized swathes of Yemeni territory in recent weeks and has left hundreds dead. In the face of such attacks and with no support from its American ally, what are Saudi Arabia’s options?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb76ca76-b4ed-11f1-a8aa-071222e1b868</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:24:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'NAZA' documentary about Gaza war sparks political storm in Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel</link><description>
The Israeli filmmakers behind the documentary NAZA may have received a standing ovation at the Venice film festival, they have been facing violent threats to their lives and citizenship at home in Israel. A month ahead of crucial elections, the film profiles anonymous military sources who speak about the widespread killing of civilians in Gaza. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers". Details by Shirli Sitbon, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd909d7e-b4ec-11f1-8bfb-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-133404-134124-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd909d7e-b4ec-11f1-8bfb-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-133404-134124-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3300ac6-b4ec-11f1-bc19-e91039182cf6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:22:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why doesn't the US intervene to defend Saudi Arabia against the Houthis?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis</link><description>
The US cautioned against a rapidly escalating situation in Yemen after Houthi rebels carried out a missile attack on the Saudi capital. In recent weeks, the Iran backed militants have also seized large portions of Yemeni territory following clashes with Saudi-backed government forces. The US is a very close ally to Saudi Arabia. Yet, is visibly unwilling to intervene on its behalf – why? Details and analysis by H. A. Hellyer, senior fellow in geopolitics at the Royal United Institute in Cairo.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce5cada-b4eb-11f1-98b6-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-130940-132125-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce5cada-b4eb-11f1-98b6-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-130940-132125-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3855050a-b4ed-11f1-a96c-07e2d7a5aa9a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:20:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>North Korea fires two ballistic missiles into the sea in latest weapons display</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260920-north-korea-fires-two-ballistic-missiles-into-the-sea-in-latest-weapons-display</link><description>
North Korea fired two short-range ballistic missiles into the sea off its eastern coast on Sunday, South Korea’s military said. This came days after Pyongyang reaffirmed its status as a nuclear-armed state and rejected a UN resolution calling for an end to its nuclear activities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75838ad2-b4e3-11f1-8ac0-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263309350737.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75838ad2-b4e3-11f1-8ac0-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263309350737.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d479b276-b4e5-11f1-97cd-058a9d6433f5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:40:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75838ad2-b4e3-11f1-8ac0-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263309350737.jpg">© Ahn Young-joon, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: Could regional polls force Friedrich Merz to step down?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-could-regional-polls-froce-friedrich-merz-to-step-down</link><description>
Polling is underway in the German capital Berlin and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania for regional elections. Both elections are seen as a test for Germany's centre-right Chancellor Friedrich Merz. He has already scheduled a crisis meeting and decided to skip this week's UN General Assembly to deal with the potential fallout. Could he be forced to step down based on the election’s results? Details and analysis by Yann Wernert, senior policy fellow at the Jacques Delors Centre in Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7241ef7c-b4dd-11f1-a7e3-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-090118-091249-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7241ef7c-b4dd-11f1-a7e3-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-090118-091249-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78326d26-b4dd-11f1-90d4-2dedec0bd379</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:26:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine hits Russia with major drone attack, targetting refinery</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hits-russia-with-major-drone-attack-targetting-refinery</link><description>
In Russia, voters are on the third and final day of casting ballots in the country's first wartime parliamentary election. Despite the voting however, Ukraine carried out what Moscow described as the "largest ever" drone attack on the Russian capital. Kyiv reportedly fired over 1.000 drones at the country, leaving two dead in the Moscow region and inflicting damage upon an oil refinery. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fbde97c-b4be-11f1-b2c6-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T042905Z-1824787393-RC2QMNA5QBAK-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-REFINERY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fbde97c-b4be-11f1-b2c6-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T042905Z-1824787393-RC2QMNA5QBAK-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-REFINERY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b738272-b4db-11f1-924e-53fa25c99ab7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:24:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nine women found dead near Johannesburg sends shockwaves through South Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nine-women-found-dead-near-johannesburg-sends-shockwaves-through-south-africa</link><description>
Vigils, group runs and moments of silence: thousands of protesters gathered across South Africa this weekend to pay tribute to the nine women found murdered in eastern Johannesburg. In a country that records more than 60 homicides a day, the nine murders sent shockwaves through the population. Anger is mounting, and calls are growing for the government to take action. Story by Caroline Baum.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf5a0fc8-b4d9-11f1-a35a-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T210632Z-470438108-RC2ULNA6GEGV-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-CRIME.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf5a0fc8-b4d9-11f1-a35a-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T210632Z-470438108-RC2ULNA6GEGV-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-CRIME.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82f08c88-b4d9-11f1-9a32-8b51192a349f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:00:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ed Sheeran calls Gaza war catastrophic after dropping Macklemore over pro-Palestinian comments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments</link><description>
English singer Ed Sheeran opened his first show since his opener Macklemore was dropped after making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. The move sparked controversy and prompted several other support acts to drop out of the tour, publishing statements citing their support for Palestinians. While some concert goers could be seen trying to sell their tickets on Saturday, others have voiced their support for the 'Shape of You' singer. Story by Charlotte Hughes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6678406e-b4d9-11f1-b75e-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T040207Z-1831225387-RC2QMNAI21XV-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-MACKLEMORE-ED-SHEERAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6678406e-b4d9-11f1-b75e-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T040207Z-1831225387-RC2QMNAI21XV-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-MACKLEMORE-ED-SHEERAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d595b3e2-b4d8-11f1-95fd-b7167bd996cb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:57:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Three media outlets barred from the White House over 'fake news'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news</link><description>
Donald Trump has suggested that more news outlets may be barred from the White House after he announced he was banning Politico, CNN and MS NOW. On Saturday, all three outlets said that the White House confiscated their teams' press passes; they have also hinted at legal action. The ban has come under sharp criticism from press freedom advocates, as Charlotte Hughes explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17f41504-b4d8-11f1-b0a3-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-081748-081932-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17f41504-b4d8-11f1-b0a3-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-081748-081932-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d65f002-b4d8-11f1-96b2-2f9da434d941</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:55:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal</link><description>
The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63667182-b4d6-11f1-8b04-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-081031-081205-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63667182-b4d6-11f1-8b04-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-081031-081205-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">691519ee-b4d6-11f1-ae1f-b37ea51a3338</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:40:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's Houthis strike Saudi capital Riyadh for the first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time</link><description>
Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Saudi Arabia continues to intensify. On Saturday morning, a fire broke out near Riyadh's main airport after Houthis said they launched missiles and drones at Saudi Arabia. On the ground in Yemen, Houthi rebels are pushing east in their fight against Saudi-backed government forces. Story by Caroline Baum.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/264babe8-b4d4-11f1-9455-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-080551-080719-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/264babe8-b4d4-11f1-9455-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-080551-080719-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2c53d6d2-b4d4-11f1-8661-553ba78fa9bc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:38:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Argentines protest Milei's austerity, demanding higher wages and public spending</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending</link><description>
Tensions are boiling over in Argentina, where a massive wave of public anger is spilling onto the streets of the capital. Following months of aggressive economic reforms and rising household debt, hundreds took to the streets in a "March of Anger", targeting President Javier Milei's austerity agenda. Details by Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836bc8c6-b4d4-11f1-9638-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-080821-080959-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836bc8c6-b4d4-11f1-9638-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-080821-080959-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">88b76754-b4d4-11f1-96cb-05f55abffce6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:38:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will German's far right party AfD win over two more regions?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/will-german-s-far-right-party-afd-win-over-two-more-regions</link><description>
Two weeks after the far-right AfD won its first major regional election in Germany, two more eastern states vote this Sunday. Polls have just opened in the capital, Berlin, and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Berlin, Jörg Taszman.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7190e544-b4d6-11f1-bbc5-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154724Z-1958111571-RC23LNAVC6LP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-MERZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7190e544-b4d6-11f1-bbc5-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154724Z-1958111571-RC23LNAVC6LP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-MERZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d61c38a4-b4d3-11f1-bc01-f962a54c6b9f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:35:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Ligue 1: Paris Saint-Germain head to Marseille for a tense Classique</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260920-ligue-1-paris-saint-germain-head-to-marseille-for-a-tense-classique</link><description>
Paris Saint-Germain will travel to Marseille this Sunday to face OM at the Vélodrome in the final game of Matchday 5 in Ligue 1. It is a must-not-lose clash between two struggling sides, both looking to use this huge fixture to kick-start their seasons.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b6a712c-b492-11f1-941d-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-372P8CV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b6a712c-b492-11f1-941d-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-372P8CV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">990d1fc4-b496-11f1-817c-290de473fefb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:34:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Russian election enters final day after major Ukrainian drone attack on Moscow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-live-russian-election-enters-final-day-in-shadow-of-war-in-ukraine</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">4fd477fe-b4c2-11f1-ad90-d93e76be58a2</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 07:10:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russian election enters final day after Kyiv targets Moscow in massive drone attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-live-russian-election-enters-final-day-in-shadow-of-war-in-ukraine</link><description>
Ukraine launched what Moscow’s Mayor Sergei Sobyanin described on Sunday as the “largest ever” attack on the Russian capital, killing two people and damaging part of an oil refinery. The major attack comes on the third and final day of voting in Russia’s first wartime parliamentary election. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.    
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad29a23c-b4e8-11f1-bbcc-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T080755Z-1641565567-RC2VMNAVR4TB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-MOSCOW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad29a23c-b4e8-11f1-bbcc-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T080755Z-1641565567-RC2VMNAVR4TB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-MOSCOW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a6beeb8-b4b2-11f1-8711-b95734b6451c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 05:16:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad29a23c-b4e8-11f1-bbcc-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T080755Z-1641565567-RC2VMNAVR4TB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-MOSCOW.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Merz under pressure as two more German states hold elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germans-vote-in-elections-threatening-fresh-blow-to-merz</link><description>
Germans began voting Sunday in two closely watched state elections that could deliver fresh gains for the far-right and far-left, piling pressure on Chancellor Friedrich Merz as he struggles with low approval ratings and tensions within his governing coalition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815009e2-b4bd-11f1-b531-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263230529590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815009e2-b4bd-11f1-b531-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263230529590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1996492c-b492-11f1-ac6a-af9a874d6e90</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:25:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815009e2-b4bd-11f1-b531-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263230529590.jpg">© Markus Schreiber, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Pop, Protests & Palestine: Ed Sheeran’s Moral Maze]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-pop-protests-palestine-ed-sheeran-s-moral-maze</link><description>
A clash over music, politics and Palestine is putting freedom of expression in the spotlight. Macklemore’s outspoken support for Palestinians has sparked a backlash around Ed Sheeran’s US tour, raising a bigger question: should artists be expected to take a political stand, or are they equally free to stay silent? France 24’s Gavin Lee is joined by Dr Adam Behr, Reader in Music, Politics and Society at Newcastle University, to discuss the controversy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49bfb17c-b471-11f1-8550-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17709532116aaefee0653b36-29870223.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49bfb17c-b471-11f1-8550-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17709532116aaefee0653b36-29870223.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f22ee952-b473-11f1-9ea2-bf8006233677</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:49:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French police arrest two Germans after 'for fun' Louvre stunt in Mona Lisa hall</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260919-two-arrested-for-louvre-stunt-for-fun-in-mona-lisa-hall</link><description>
Two Germans were arrested Saturday after they stuck two paintings on a wall of the hall that hosts the Mona Lisa in Paris's Louvre Museum, police sources said. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18ada5bc-b46c-11f1-8251-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2U84CB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18ada5bc-b46c-11f1-8251-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2U84CB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc35539a-b46a-11f1-8fba-513005dadc78</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:45:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18ada5bc-b46c-11f1-8251-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2U84CB.jpg">© Lou Benoist, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron and Carney to hold talks on strengthening Canada-France ties</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260919-french-outpost-off-canada-in-the-spotlight-as-macron-hosts-carney-on-symbolic-visit</link><description>
